"The patient underwent robot-assisted radical prostatectomy with a pathological stage pT2, negative surgical margins, no seminal vesicle invasion, absence of lymphovascular invasion, and no lymph node metastasis. The preoperative PSA was 5. The biopsy revealed a Gleason 4+4 pattern in the left peripheral zone (base) with a cribriform pattern. These favorable pathological findings, including negative margins and no nodal metastasis, are positive prognostic factors. Countervailing factors include the preoperative PSA of 5 and the discrepancy between the biopsy grade (Gleason 4+4) and the prostatectomy grade (Gleason 3+4, ISUP grade group 2). Missing postoperative PSA or follow-up data currently widens the uncertainty regarding the trajectory. Information regarding postoperative PSA and its subsequent trajectory would be crucial to revise the prognosis. The fixed estimated horizon is 31.06 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 24.85–37.27 months; its coverage has not been validated."
